#!/usr/bin/env node
// t3blackout: build upstream T3 Code with every phone-home stripped.
//
//   t3blackout update [--ref <tag|branch|sha>] [--channel nightly|preview|stable] [--force] [--stage-only] [--unpinned]
//                     [--expect-sha SHA]   the app's download: build only if SHA is still the approved release
//   t3blackout check  [--ref ...] [--build]   apply strip rules to the pinned release (--ref: any) without
//                                      installing; --build also builds, scans and smoke-tests it
//   t3blackout drift                   open what upstream changed under the features a build left out
//   t3blackout preview [--installed]   try the staged build in a sandboxed window before restarting into it
//   t3blackout review [--installed]    gather the staged build's report and upstream commits for an agent
//   t3blackout poll [--offline]        is a newer upstream release available?
//   t3blackout apply [--wait-pid N] [--expect-sha SHA --expect-blackout SHA]
//                                      install a staged build once the app has quit (only the expected one), relaunch it
//   t3blackout smoke                   re-run the zero-egress smoke test on the last build
//   t3blackout launch                  open the installed app (installs a staged build first)
//   t3blackout status                  installed version, schedule, build account, signing
//   t3blackout rollback                swap back to the previously installed build
//   t3blackout schedule [--day hourly|daily|monday] [--hour 4] | unschedule   hourly (default), daily or weekly
//   t3blackout configure [--role ui|host|both]   save the install's role and locations (install.sh runs it;
//                                      a changed role moves the scheduled job at the next `schedule`)
//   t3blackout signing adopt|import|init|status [--vault V]   macOS: shared signing identity via 1Password
//   t3blackout evaluate [--channel nightly] [--ref TAG] [--baseline TAG] [--build] [--write] [--report FILE] [--resolved DIR]
//                       [--stage-from DIR]
//                                      CI: pin the newest upstream release that passes every gate
//   t3blackout pin-check [--candidate FILE --channel C --resolved DIR --result FILE]
//                                      CI: re-derive a candidate pin's gates before it is signed
//                                      (alone: check each pinned tag still names its commit upstream)
//   t3blackout advisories --channel C --resolved DIR --out FILE   CI: advisories against main's pin
//   t3blackout releases --channel C [--out FILE]   CI: upstream releases newer than main's pin
//
// With pin.json (proposed by the evaluator in CI, re-checked here by self-update),
// every machine builds the pinned release for its channel, and a channel pin.json
// doesn't pin is refused unless --unpinned is given. Without a pin.json, or with
// --unpinned on a channel it doesn't pin, releases are built once they're
// --soak-hours old (default 48), with none of the evaluator's gates; --unpinned
// never bypasses a channel's pin.
// Fetching and building run as the separate build account when install.sh set one up.
//
// A feature whose rules no longer match upstream is left out of the build
// (lib/features.mjs) and the update goes ahead; a strict rule (privacy, identity,
// the updater) that no longer matches holds the update at the newest release it
// still applies to.

